13:Teda,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does it mean to get mentioned by LLMs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When someone asks ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Claude or Google AI Overviews for advice - \"what is the best tool for X\", \"which brand should I pick\" - the answer names a handful of brands. Getting mentioned by LLMs means your brand is one of those names, or your page is one of the sources the answer links to."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do AI assistants decide which brands to mention?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Assistants that search the web before answering lean on pages that already rank for the question, and on what other sites say about a brand. A brand that has clear, useful pages on the topic and shows up in articles and roundups on other domains gives the model both an answer to quote and a reason to trust it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why use Outrank to get mentioned by LLMs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Because it does the steady work that AI mentions are built on, without you hiring a content team or doing outreach. It works in two ways. On your own blog, we research keywords, write and publish 30 SEO-optimized articles a month on the questions your customers ask, so there is a page of yours worth quoting. On other blogs, our Backlinks service places full articles about you on sites that already get Google traffic, so the web talks about you, not only you about yourself."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you guarantee that ChatGPT will recommend my brand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, and you should be wary of anyone who does. Nobody outside the AI companies controls what their models say. What we do is build the groundwork those answers are made from: content that ranks and mentions on other sites. Outrank customers like AIApply report being picked up in AI answers after publishing with us, but results depend on your niche, competition and how long you keep going."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to show up in AI answers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There is no fixed timeline. New articles first need to be indexed and start ranking, and mentions on other sites add up over weeks and months. The earlier you start, the sooner AI assistants find you among the sources they already lean on."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need the Backlinks plan, or is the main plan enough?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The main plan already covers your own content and builds backlinks for you. The Backlinks service goes further: a full article on a DR 30+ blog with 100+ organic clicks a month, a 250-350 word section about you inside it, and first place when the article is a roundup. It runs on the Scale plan at $899/month, and every link is re-checked for 90 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will AI trust articles written with AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AI assistants care about whether a page answers the question well, not about who typed it. Every Outrank article is built on researched facts with source links, checked before it publishes, and written in your brand voice with a clear structure. You can read, edit or rewrite any article before it goes live."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which languages and platforms do you support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We write in 150+ languages and publish automatically to WordPress, Webflow, Shopify, Wix, Framer, Notion, Ghost, Next.js or any platform through a webhook."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I try it first?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The main plan starts with a 3-day free trial, and you can cancel anytime - no questions asked."}}]}16:T912,
